  "style_decision": {
    "what_style_E_is": "(1) Cold open is a WHAT-IF, not a statement — the withheld thing is the promise, its arrival is the payoff. (2) Teaching register signposted throughout («यहाँ ध्यान दीजिए» / «Notice this», «Think of it this way», «Work it through»). (3) One analogy introduced early that PAYS OFF LATER, so a later beat lands as a callback rather than a new idea. (4) Arithmetic stepped across lines, never compressed into one.",
    "reference_scripts": "studio/voice-tests/passive-income-number/style-E-teacher-curiosity.txt (hi ch1-2) and style-E-en-teacher-curiosity.txt (en ch1-2). Both are ch1+ch2 only — chapters 3+ must be restyled to match, keeping their facts and structure unchanged.",
    "line_1_7_en_is_untouchable": "«Everyone asks how much you need invested to live off dividends, and the honest answer costs more than the popular one.» It is the title's own promise and the phrase this format ranks on."
